WEBVTT

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.660
After the entrance exams are over,
the students wait impatiently for two weeks.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.750
To get the results list, one of the examinees

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:48.690
visit the post office everyday
to pick up the Charlottetown Daily.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:55.890
I feel uneasy. I'm sure that the announcement
of the results will be out today.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:59.200
You're right. It should have been
published two days ago, after all.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.660
Ruby, if your name is not on the list,
what do you intend to do?

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.970
Josie, don't say such horrible things!
You know I'm most worried about this.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:10.810
It'll be fine, Ruby.
I'm sure all of us have passed.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.780
I feel much better hearing you say that, Jane.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.510
Oh! But what if I don't make it?

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.680
Oh, Anne and the others are here.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:25.920
Is the newspaper here yet?

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.050
No, not yet.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.070
Can I leave for a while?

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.100
Sure.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.590
How is it? Any news today?

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:01.960
I don't know.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.550
I only loaded them and brought
them directly from the station.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.470
Then hurry up. I have a feeling
the results will be out today.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.570
How can I hurry on this type of slope?

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:13.970
Charlie, let's help to push.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:14.980
Okay.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:22.670
Hey! You'll scare the horse! Don't be reckless!

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.260
They're here! They're here!

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:38.460
You're right.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.050
Stop... stop...

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.450
We're taking out Avonlea's mail.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.090
Sure, that's fine. Sorry to trouble you.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.160
Well, they're here waiting today as well.
Thank you for your hard work.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:10.980
Yes.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.430
Please hurry and let us see
the newspaper, Mr. McNeil!

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.700
All right, let me get one out for you.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:43.230
It's not published today either.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:48.600
This is horrible! Are we supposed to wait forever?!

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.970
You're right. How many times do
we have to feel this way?

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.840
I can't be helped. Let's come again tomorrow.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.490
We should have learned to
take it easy like Moody.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.980
What's with Moody?

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:04.320
He seems halfway through to giving up.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.270
Moody, the results weren't announced today either.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.050
Great! Thanks for telling me.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.640
I hope that the results
will never be announced.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:34.010
I envy you your calmness in going to
the post office for the newspaper everyday.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.810
I don't have that kind of courage.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.800
Oh, none of us are calm.
We go there because we're worried.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:42.210
You may be right,

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:46.090
but no matter whether I make it or not,

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:49.030
I've decided to stay at home
and wait for the news.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:49.820
Now then...

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:17.380
Three weeks have passed, and everyone
is still waiting for the announcement of the results.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.350
To Anne and the others,
the tension is almost unbearable.

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:39.050
Oh my, Anne Shirley!

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.030
What's wrong?

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.710
Don't tell me...

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.480
The announcement hasn't been
published today either, Mrs. Allan.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.800
I wonder what happened.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.130
In the past, the announcement
would have been published by now.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:54.620
That's right. Everyone's going crazy.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.150
Anyway, please come inside.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:04.260
I can understand how all
of you must be feeling.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:08.680
But no matter how you worry,
you can't change the results.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.640
Yes, I know that.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:18.020
Worrying about this every day and
spending your days in anxiety

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.950
won't make the announcement of
the results come any sooner.

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:24.360
Don't you think this is a waste of
your long-awaited summer vacation?

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:25.690
But...

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:36.730
I guess it's hard to ask you to forget
about the announcement of the results,

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:38.360
but even if you have to force yourself,

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:42.740
try to busy yourself with something
every day to make your days richer.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:50.250
So why don't you try to enjoy
every day as much as you can?

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:51.690
Every day...

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:56.700
Yes. Then you'll feel the day of the
announcement will come faster.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:00.530
You should stop going to the post office.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.160
Look.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.650
It looks like there was no
announcement today either.

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:33.990
I'm starting to wonder when
the announcement will be made.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.670
Well, the head of education is a conservative.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:42.140
They have no sympathy
for those poor children.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:44.100
You're right.

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:50.170
At the next election, I may decide
to vote for the Liberal Party.

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:20.370
You haven't finished yet?

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:21.200
No.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.550
What's wrong?

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:24.380
I have no appetite.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:27.610
You hardly eat anything recently.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.880
I understand how you feel,

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:34.400
but won't ruining your health only ensure
that you can't go to Queen's Academy?

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:38.600
I know, but I really can't eat.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:44.630
You've been sitting around listlessly all day.
Of course you don't feel hungry.

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:48.630
You did nothing but go to the post
office these past days, right?

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:52.820
Why don't you work on your
patchwork or give me a hand?

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:57.340
You're right. I think I should do that, too.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:00.250
Yesterday, Mrs. Allan gave me some advice, too.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:03.410
She wanted me to busy myself with something.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:04.210
But...

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.980
But you just can't bring
yourself to do anything, right?

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:07.910
I'm sorry.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:14.940
Oh yes! What do you think
about going out to the field?

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:19.820
You should go and help Matthew dry the hay.

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:21.530
I'm not sure you can be of help,

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.460
but I think at least it will make you hungry.

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:27.440
Marilla, that's a great idea!

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.910
I've always wanted to try it once,

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:36.540
but you always said it's not proper for
a girl to help with a man's work.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:37.980
This is an exception.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:42.120
I'm really tired of looking
at your lifeless face.

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:45.430
Finish up your food and go.
Matthew will be pleased.

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.530
I will. Thank you, Marilla.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:35.090
Anne!

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:38.280
Anne! Here's your lunch!

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.150
Thank you.

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.030
Please go ahead.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:43.590
Anne is more at peace than
she has been in a long while.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:46.270
Maybe it is because of a full day's work.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:49.560
There's no room for her to think
about the announcement of the results.

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:53.280
She is too hungry, tired and sleepy.

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:04.450
However, that night, Anne
falls dramatically on her bed

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.570
without even changing her clothes.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:10.590
Her face shows peace which
comes from the release of her worry.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:47.710
Matthew, you've thought that it would
be better if I were a boy sometimes, right?

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:52.630
That way, I could help you with more work, right? So...

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:55.680
Well, now...

00:13:55.720 --> 00:14:01.390
I never thought of wanting
a boy after you came.

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:03.520
Is it true, Matthew?

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:11.530
Well, now... Of course.
Why are you asking this?

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:24.210
I never thought of asking
you to help me in the fields.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:28.540
Yes, but I had so much fun yesterday.

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:33.210
I got very tired, but I fell asleep
without a thought after dinner.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:38.050
Well, now. It's good to
do it now and then.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:43.680
But you shouldn't push yourself too hard.
Why don't you stop for the day?

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:45.990
Oh, I'm fine, because I...

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:49.280
No. You can help me tomorrow as well.

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:52.480
Better that you don't
take on too much at once.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:56.710
All right. But you must let me
help you tomorrow.

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:12.040
Oh, I see... Matthew's right, too.

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:15.830
You never know your
limits when you do things.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:18.760
If you suddenly work too intensely, you might collapse.

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:21.810
Oh! But Marilla, you're the one who suggested it.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.100
I know...

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:26.420
Well, you've picked enough now.

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:31.170
I'm going over to Rachel to deliver these.

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:32.530
You should stay at home.

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:35.430
I can bring those over to Mrs. Lynde.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:38.180
It's all right. I need to talk to her.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.350
I see.

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:41.700
You should take a short break
before preparing the tea.

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:39.710
Anne! Anne!

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:44.370
Diana!

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:47.020
Anne, I'm coming up!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.480
Anne, you passed! You're in first place, too!

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:09.610
You and Gilbert were tied,
but your name was first.

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:12.110
Oh! I'm so happy for you!

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.900
You did just splendidly, Anne!

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:11.400
My father brought the newspaper from
Bright River less than 10 minutes ago.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:15.770
It came out on the afternoon train, you know,
and won't be here till tomorrow by mail.

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:18.970
When I saw the pass list,
I just rushed over like a wild thing.

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:23.330
You've all passed, even Moody Spurgeon,
although he's conditioned in history.

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:25.980
Jane and Ruby did pretty well,

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.540
they're halfway up,

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:29.220
and so did Charlie.

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:32.090
Josie managed to scrape through
with three marks to spare,

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:35.100
but she's bragging like
she passed as number one.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.500
Miss Stacy will be so happy.

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:43.240
Anne, how does it feel to be first?

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:46.430
If it were me, I know I'd go crazy with joy.

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:48.740
I am pretty near crazy as it is,

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:52.580
but you're as calm and
cool as a spring evening.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.580
Diana, I don't feel calm.

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:59.450
I want to say so much, but I
can't find the words to say them in.

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:02.120
I never dreamed of this...

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.790
No, I did too. Just once.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:09.760
'What if I should come out first?',
I thought while shivering.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:11.130
But that's what happened, right?

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:14.100
I had the best grades of everyone from this island!

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:17.330
Just the thought of it
makes me feel I am arrogant.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:18.930
Wait, Diana.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:21.600
I must run right out to
the field to tell Matthew.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:27.910
Then we'll go up the road and
tell the good news to the others!

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:32.310
Yes! I'm coming with you.
Because your joy is my joy!

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:35.950
Thank you, Diana!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.260
Matthew! Matthew!

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:46.630
I passed! I passed!

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:48.900
Oh, looks like the results are out.

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:55.400
I've passed and I'm first,
or one of the first!

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:56.810
Please look here!

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:01.770
I'm not vain, but I'm very thankful!

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.940
You're really first?

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:15.790
Well now, I always said it.
I knew you could beat them all easy.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:17.700
Matthew...

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:23.540
Anne, you've done pretty well, I must say.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:27.790
This is great. I sincerely think so!

00:20:28.280 --> 00:20:31.640
Anne, you're our glory.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:33.550
I feel so honoured.

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:36.350
Thank you, Mrs. Lynde.

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:40.820
The others have passed, too.
We're going to tell them now.

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:42.290
- See you! Let's go!
- Yes!

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:50.320
I'm going, too. I'm going to tell
everyone in the village this big news.

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:58.530
Anne did really well.

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:00.230
Yes.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.030
The day after the announcement of
the results has been made,

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.390
all the students of the Queen's class
gather at the pastor's home.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:21.250
Mr. And Mrs. Allan has invited all the successful candidates.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:44.620
You all look so mature today,
like gentlemen and ladies.

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:49.690
If even one of us had failed, I don't think
we would have been able to smile like this.

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:51.000
Of course.

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:56.650
We're celebrating all of you today.
Please take your time when you eat.

00:21:56.700 --> 00:22:02.330
Oh yes. Let's have a toast to wish
everyone a bright future.

00:22:02.370 --> 00:22:03.860
Of course, with this tea.

00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:06.340
This is really great.

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:13.680
Cheers.

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:15.080
Cheers!

00:22:15.650 --> 00:22:16.760
It's so hot.

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:25.300
Actually, Miss Stacy sent a telegram to congratulate you.

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:30.520
Miss Stacy seems to have done
a good job, don't you think?

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:33.010
Yes. This is all thanks to her.

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:34.820
That's true.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:36.050
Well then, I'll read it to you.

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:40.140
"Dear students of Queen's Class,"

00:22:40.170 --> 00:22:44.010
"I sincerely congratulate everyone on passing."

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:47.560
"Please become good role models of Avonlea from now on.

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:51.540
"I will always be with you.
Muriel Stacy."

00:22:54.660 --> 00:22:57.020
It's just as Miss Stacy says.

00:22:57.060 --> 00:22:59.990
You mustn't forget the feeling of gratitude
you have towards your teacher today.

00:23:00.250 --> 00:23:04.560
And I want you to work hard to
reach your respective goals from now on.

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:09.800
Of course, you mustn't forget to
thank your parents and the Lord.

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:39.430
Miss Stacy, we're so grateful to you.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:53.340
That evening, Anne kneels sweetly by her open
window in a great sheen of moonshine,

00:23:53.910 --> 00:23:57.980
and murmurs a prayer of gratitude and
aspiration that comes straight from her heart.

00:23:59.590 --> 00:24:06.360
There is in it thankfulness for the
past and reverent petition for the future.

00:24:18.440 --> 00:24:24.210
Anne prepares to recite before all the
well-dressed people, with a nervous heart.

00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:27.070
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 40

00:24:27.620 --> 00:24:29.150
The Hotel Concert

00:24:29.180 --> 00:24:30.670
Please look forward to it!
